# Response headers for the static pages, applied by Workers Static Assets.
# The Worker sets its own headers on /api/* and /admin*, so these rules do not
# reach the contact API or the admin screen.
#
# The pages share their origin with the admin screen. A script on any page
# runs with the authority of a signed-in admin, so the Content Security Policy
# allows scripts only from this site and from Cloudflare Turnstile (the
# contact form's bot check). Astro writes every script to /_astro/
# (astro.config.ts), so 'unsafe-inline' is not needed for scripts.
# style-src-attr allows only the style attribute on <html> that sets the
# theme colors from site.config.ts; <style> elements and other inline styles
# are not allowed. If you add a script, an embed, analytics, or a font
# service, add its origin here on purpose, and read AGENTS.md first.
#
# Strict-Transport-Security is not set here. A browser that has seen it
# refuses plain HTTP until max-age passes, so a wrong value cannot be taken
# back quickly. Turn on "Always Use HTTPS" (and HSTS, if you want it) for
# your zone in the Cloudflare dashboard instead.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; connect-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()

/sitemap.xml
  Content-Type: application/xml; charset=utf-8
